], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 45219, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QBawudGC5UqhvXEiF2zqUU", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 47443, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01GGJXwjAt6UtBh6nMcjFA5y", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 47743, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GGJXwjAt6UtBh6nMcjFA5y", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 47743, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GGJXwjAt6UtBh6nMcjFA5y", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 52690, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n1. **Rollback:** The live version, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its pre-release build, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy. The most recent healthy release was v2.3.0, and all three regions are now running it. After the rollback the service passes health checks and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n2. **Incident:** The request to create the SEV2 incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had gone through, so I didn't retry. That way on-call isn't paged twice. INC-0001 describes the failure and the rollback. It also says the next steps are to find the cause of the v2.3.1 problem and not to redeploy v2.3.1 until it's fixed.\n\nThe incident text still lists checking recovery as a next step, but I've already confirmed it. No approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had been healthy in production before.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "